id: pm-graph-triplicate
title: Render package visuals with build-time Triplicate tokens
description: "Restyle every diagram format from pinned pm-brand values; preserve export behavior and prove light/dark accessibility with real tracker renders, regression and revert evidence."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T09:27:51.195Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:09:05.521Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:08:57.642Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:08:57.642Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Reverified main f46704ef4083 (unchanged since audit): [PR #145](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/pull/145) (4c4ac08) styles exported graph diagrams from pinned build-time pm-brand values. Retained evidence: scripts/brand-values.ts, src/brand-values.ts, src/brand.ts."
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:28:13.055Z",codex-agent,"Design: form-paper canvas and ruled top sheets; carbon text, Martian Mono ids and dates, explicit status labels and contract chip fills. Canary and rose only convey in_progress and blocked. Brand values are generated at build time from an exact devDependency; published runtime has no brand dependency or CDN fetches. Existing scheduling, graph edges and serialization stay intact."
  "2026-10-17T10:12:53.675Z",codex-agent,"Visual formats are Mermaid flowcharts, DOT and PlantUML; interchange schemas remain unchanged. Each uses ruled sheets, a real mono form strip and explicit filled/outlined status cells. DOT/PlantUML accept literal dark palettes through renderer arguments; Mermaid adapts scoped CSS. Browser review caught ignored directives and variables rejected in Mermaid source style declarations; these now use a leading directive, scoped CSS values and a literal border declaration. Behavioral revert proof restores only each of the three renderers in turn: the unchanged real-tracker regression fails 1/1 each; the restored implementation passes 1/1. The README embeds pm-brand banner commit 5c80a2b707f3a00afe986e81e520843b86f3ee83. Full gates are pending."
  "2026-10-17T10:50:59.381Z",codex-agent,"Render review caught a Mermaid canvas rule rejected because bare declarations preceded it. Removed the invalid declarations and themed nested edge-label backgrounds. Real-tracker focused tests pass 5/5; scoped renderer revert proofs remain 1/1 failures for each of Mermaid, DOT and PlantUML, with 1/1 passes restored. Full computed-color browser checks and release gates are being rerun on the corrected implementation."
  "2026-10-17T11:29:18.305Z",codex-agent,"Both CI-isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass: each 352/352 tests; 99.72% lines, 95.24% branches and 100% functions over all 13 intended runtime sources, zero failed, canceled or skipped tests. The pinned pm runner passes focused tests 5/5; project test execution tracking remains disabled by existing policy, so results are recorded here. Published 72 before/after PNGs on pr-screenshots, with 36 after cases passing widths/themes/scales, no overflow, animations, interactive actions or external requests. Renderer hashes match the published evidence. Independent renderer reverts fail 1/1 each and restored renderers pass 1/1. Strict CI-isolated tracker health passes with existing advisories retained. CI retains Node 22 coverage and runs both full release gates on Node 26 without a redundant third coverage run. No brand token gap found; pm-brand release remains held. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress."
  "2026-10-17T11:35:00.919Z",codex-agent,"CI on Bun 1.4.3 failed before the full release checks: npm-lock migration compared the Git kit download with npm prepared-archive integrity. A fresh-cache minimal reproduction fails with the original entry and passes when only that optional integrity field is removed. The exact approved commit and all registry dependency integrity values stay pinned. Applying this lock-only repair and validating fresh npm and Bun installs; renderer values and published PNGs remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-17T11:39:41.152Z",codex-agent,"Fresh npm ci and clean-cache Bun 1.4.3 install both pass after removing only the optional integrity field from the exact Git dependency. brand:check and a fresh build pass; committed dist and renderer hashes are unchanged. The original lock entry reproduces IntegrityCheckFailed, while the commit-only entry installs successfully. Registry integrity checks remain intact. Full npm/Bun runtime gate evidence is unchanged; CI will rerun both complete release gates on this installation-metadata repair. Kit release remains held."
  "2026-10-17T11:46:26.299Z",codex-agent,"Windows CI exposed a separate kit portability gap: its Git prepare invokes the extensionless TypeScript shim. The Windows lifecycle job now installs locked artifacts without dependency scripts and invokes this package's real prepare through npm/cmd.exe. Its strict driver-health, adversarial Windows-parser and coverage-path checks stay unchanged; Linux full lifecycle installs and npm/Bun release gates stay intact. Follow-up pm-graph-brand-windows tracks the kit repair and removal of this workaround. No renderer or token value changed."
  "2026-10-17T11:55:44.181Z",codex-agent,"Windows npm 10.9.9 still prepares Git dependencies despite the ignore-scripts flag, so the scoped Windows installation now invokes the tested npm 11.17.0 explicitly. The package prepare remains an npm/cmd.exe invocation with unchanged health/parser/coverage assertions. DeepScan treated truthiness checks on already-normalized string statuses as null checks; DOT and PlantUML now test the empty string explicitly. All six light/dark visual sources match the published render inputs byte-for-byte, recorded in docs/triplicate-browser-checks.json. Focused real-tracker/parity tests pass 5/5. Kit Windows portability remains the documented follow-up; no visual output or coverage threshold changed."
  "2026-10-18T03:00:31.788Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: both newest CodeRabbit findings are valid. Emit one explicit Mermaid token theme and escape extensible PlantUML status labels inside Creole cells. Add independent behavioral regressions and function-only revert proofs; retain all gate thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T03:07:38.759Z",codex-agent,"Additional issue 146 reproduced at the HTML-label escape path. Add literal backslash escaping and explicit BR elements for titles, strips and status cells, exercised with local Graphviz WASM because the native dot binary is unavailable. Consolidate revert probes in the existing harness to preserve zero duplication."
  "2026-10-18T03:35:08.346Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 evidence: all three review/issue function-only reverts fail their retained regression independently, then pass when restored. The focused renderer file passes 4/4. Browser captures cover all three visual formats at 1440/768/390 in both themes; all 18 after cases have no overflow, motion or interactive actions and zero external requests. Mermaid paper is checked against its selected theme. Main-based before and updated after evidence is under pr-screenshots/brand/triplicate-visuals/round2."
  "2026-10-18T03:42:51.999Z",codex-agent,"Prepared all requested renderer fixes and revert proofs. Typecheck, lint, 0% duplication and focused 4/4 tests pass. Full local release validation under heavy resource contention has an existing Neo4j connection-error timing assertion failure; its 5-second threshold is unchanged. Push the prepared tree for exact-head CI validation, then record complete gate receipts before handoff."
  "2026-10-18T03:53:29.226Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI run 39094633261 at 3b24e69ac4b78d5c255a924c9fafce373a4bbb65 passes Node 22, Node 26 and the Windows lifecycle job. Node 26 npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 355/355 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/TODOs; coverage is 99.72% lines, 95.25% branches and 100% functions across all 13 gated sources. Thresholds remain unchanged. Three independent function reverts fail 1/1 each and restored functions pass 1/1 each; focused renderer suite passes 4/4. The unchanged local Neo4j timing control passes 1/1 in isolation; resource-contention full local runs are not counted as passing and were stopped after complete CI gates passed. No threads are resolved and no release occurs. Release ownership for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
